        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Oh, I see - usual log in ~/.cache/qTox/qtox.log got much bigger size)\nThere I see related strings:\n```\n...\n[14:07:06.807 UTC] (tox.core) network.c:1958 : Debug: connecting socket 33 to 172.105.109.31:33445\n[14:07:06.807 UTC] (tox.core) network.c:1958 : Debug: connecting socket 35 to 3.0.24.15:33445\n[14:07:06.808 UTC] (tox.core) network.c:1958 : Debug: connecting socket 36 to <my_node_IP>:3389\n...\n[14:07:12.772 UTC] (default) src/core/core.cpp:354 : Debug: Connecting to bootstrap node \"<my_node_PBK>\"\n[14:07:17.037 UTC] (default) src/core/core.cpp:313 : Debug: Connected to the UDP DHT\n...\n[14:12:54.288 UTC] (default) src/net/bootstrapnodeupdater.cpp:162 : Debug: Loaded 38 bootstrap nodes from \":/conf/nodes.json\"\n...\n[14:13:01.072 UTC] (default) src/net/bootstrapnodeupdater.cpp:162 : Debug: Loaded 1 bootstrap nodes from \"~/.config/tox/bootstrapNodes.json\"\n[14:13:01.072 UTC] (default) src/net/bootstrapnodeupdater.cpp:226 : Debug: User bootstrap nodes file found at \"~/.config/tox/bootstrapNodes.json\"\n[14:13:01.072 UTC] (default) src/net/bootstrapnodeupdater.cpp:162 : Debug: Loaded 1 bootstrap nodes from \"~/.config/tox/bootstrapNodes.json\"\n[14:13:01.072 UTC] (default) src/core/core.cpp:353 : Debug: Connecting to bootstrap node \"<my_node_PBK>\"\n[14:13:04.334 UTC] (default) src/core/core.cpp:312 : Debug: Connected to the UDP DHT\n```\nLooks strange to me that qTox first connects to my node (at 14:07:17.037), and only then founds file with it (14:13:01.072) and connects again (14:13:04.334)...\nNevertheless - now my bootstrapNodes.json stays untouched! \nWith only one (my) node inside and exactly same 413 bytes of size as it was at qTox start. Before it was becoming 14+K after first connection, that's why this issue was created.\nThe only thing I did was removing write permission from file (now I set it back to have clean test).\n\nI have no idea why it was behaving such a way, seems that now it's gone. \n\nOnly question remains - as far as I understand, bootstrapNodes.json should be a kind of storage of actual nodes found on successfull connect, now it's not so - my sole node sits there alone. Is it right?",
